{"id": "EUVD-2026-102262", "enisaUuid": "6237210f-5c3d-39b9-a155-c0caeb43118a", "description": "libfwsi through 20260522 contains a heap out-of-bounds read vulnerability in libfwsi_mtp_volume_values_read_data() that allows attackers to read past buffer bounds via crafted MTP volume shell items. Attackers can embed a 10 to 53 byte shell item with item data size of 44 or more in a .lnk file, jump list or shell bag to crash consuming processes.", "datePublished": "2026-10-15T18:57:29", "dateUpdated": "2026-10-21T01:18:16", "baseScore": 6.9, "baseScoreVersion": "4.0", "baseScoreVector": "CVSS:4.0/AV:L/AC:L/AT:N/PR:N/UI:P/VC:L/VI:N/VA:H/SC:N/SI:N/SA:N", "references": ["https://hackmd.io/@haind-pwn/libfwsi-mtp-values-oob-read", "https://github.com/libyal/libfwsi/blob/2f2aba25b888f37314a39d8c3e71c0e3ced56e59/libfwsi/libfwsi_mtp_volume_values.c#L248-L273", "https://github.com/libyal/libfwsi", "https://www.vulncheck.com/advisories/libfwsi-through-20260522-heap-out-of-bounds-read-via-libfwsi-mtp-volume-values-read-data"], "aliases": ["CVE-2026-111135", "GHSA-7h63-p8xp-f7mw"], "assigner": "VulnCheck", "epss": 0.13, "enisaIdProduct": [{"id": "4c8b5982-721b-3f66-8716-ed7ea41a239f", "product": {"name": "libfwsi", "vendor": {"name": "libyal"}}, "product_version": "0 \u226420260522"}], "enisaIdVendor": [{"id": "5992434f-a79d-31f9-9486-3a0ace11a2e0", "vendor": {"name": "libyal"}}], "isExploited": false}